  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><img src=\"assets\\st0064_5839e9935428.png\" style=\"width: 281px; height: 200px;\" /></p><p>Equation of the tangent to the parabola can be written as <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>m</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mfenced><mfrac><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\"><mn>1</mn></mstyle><mrow><mn>4</mn><mi>m</mi></mrow></mfrac></mfenced></math> or <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>m</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>4</mn><mi>m</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p><p>Now, the perpendicular distance from <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;to the tangent is equal to the radius of the given circle, so<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>O</mi><mi>M</mi><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt><mo>&#8658;</mo><mfenced close=\"|\" open=\"|\"><mfrac><mfrac><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><mi>m</mi></mrow></mfrac><msqrt><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>m</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></msqrt></mfrac></mfenced><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mn>2</mn><mfenced><mrow><mn>16</mn><msup><mi>m</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfenced><mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>m</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#160;&#160;</mo><mo>&#8658;</mo><mn>32</mn><msup><mi>m</mi><mn>4</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>32</mn><msup><mi>m</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mo>&#160;&#160;</mo><msup><mi>m</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo>-</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mn>5</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mn>3</mn></msup><msqrt><mn>16</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></msqrt></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mn>5</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></math>&nbsp;ignoring the negative sign as it is square function.</p><p>Now&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced close=\"|\" open=\"|\"><mrow><mn>8</mn><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfenced close=\"|\" open=\"|\"><mrow><mn>8</mn><msup><mi>m</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mfenced close=\"|\" open=\"|\"><mfrac><mrow><mo>-</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mn>5</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mn>3</mn></msup><msqrt><mn>16</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></msqrt></mrow><msup><mn>2</mn><mn>3</mn></msup></mfrac></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn></math></p>"
  }
